{% layout 'default' %}
{%- comment -%}
  A single “projects” page.

  Wrapped in anatole's `.post` / `.post__content`, the same as `posts`, `pages` and
  `portfolio-items`. This is not cosmetic: every content rule the theme has —
  heading sizes, link colour, `pre`/`code`, and the Timber `:::figure` layout classes
  in `_sass/partials/components/_figure.scss` — is scoped to `.post__content`. The
  stock Timber scaffold this file used to carry (`<article class="page">`) matches no
  anatole selector at all, so a projects page got none of it and body figures ignored
  their `layout`/`size` (a `wrap-right` image rendered column-wide and unfloated).
  Keep the wrapper in step with the other type templates.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% block main %}
  <div class="post animated fadeInDown">
    <div class="post__content">
      <h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
      {{ content }}
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
